# XSH setsid()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.setsid.001
anchor     functions/setsid.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/setsid.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       A child that leads no group calls setsid(): it returns the
           child's ID, and then getpgrp() and getsid(0) in the child both
           return that ID, while the test process keeps its own group and
           session.
test       t/001-new-session.c

assertion  XSH.setsid.002
anchor     functions/setsid.html#ERRORS/EPERM
anchor     functions/setsid.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       A child that has made itself a group leader (setpgid(0, 0)) gets
           -1 with EPERM from setsid(), and its session is unchanged.
test       t/002-leader.c

assertion  XSH.setsid.003
anchor     functions/setsid.html#ERRORS/EPERM
class      required
since      1988
says       A child that is not a group leader, but whose ID is the group ID
           of its own child (it led that group and then joined the test
           process's group), gets -1 with EPERM from setsid().
test       t/003-group-in-use.c
